> Actual source diagnostics

These figures read saved outputs of the complete run above. Validation loss, task accuracy and likelihood are different quantities. Few epochs and a compact subset do not establish benchmark convergence; keep the original held-out results and baseline comparisons in view.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/bilstm_crf_validation.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){std::ifstream in("build/recovered-language/models/bilstm_crf/history.tsv");if(!in)throw std::runtime_error("original history missing");std::string line;std::getline(in,line);std::vector<double>x,y;while(std::getline(in,line)){std::istringstream row(line);double epoch,loss;if(row>>epoch>>loss){x.push_back(epoch);y.push_back(loss);}}if(x.empty())throw std::runtime_error("source validation rows missing");dm::graphics::RPlot::create().lines(x,y,"source validation loss",{37,99,235}).points(x,y,"recorded epochs",{37,99,235},5).title("bilstm crf original validation history").x_label("Epoch").y_label("Source validation objective").size(1100,600).save_svg("build/bilstm_crf_validation.svg");}
